name 'iterating-with-ai-preassessment-q4_2025'

question 'A developer writes a loop to print the numbers 1 through 10, but the program only prints 1 through 9. This is a common example of:'

wrong 'An infinite loop.'
wrong 'A syntax error.'
right 'An off-by-one error.'
wrong 'A data mutation error.'

allow_multiple_attempts false

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
Lesson 2

Off-by-one errors occur when a loop starts or stops one iteration too early or too late, often due to confusion between `<` and `<=` or array indexing.
MARKDOWN
